{"type":"data","nodes":[{"type":"data","data":[{"debug":1},true],"uses":{}},{"type":"data","data":[{"slug":1,"metadata":2,"images":111,"html":241,"xml":301},"ISic003403",{"file":1,"uri":1,"title":3,"status":4,"editions":6,"editionAuthor":19,"type":20,"support":25,"objectType":26,"material":30,"condition":36,"dimensions":38,"layoutDesc":49,"handNote":62,"date":78,"places":83,"geo":93,"country":88,"provenance":85,"provenanceFound":97,"provenanceGeo":105,"provenanceObserved":106,"provenanceLost":19,"graphics":111,"region":133,"settlement":90,"repository":134,"idno":147,"textLang":150,"bibliographyEdition":154,"bibliographyDiscussion":195,"citation":198,"tmNumber":8,"facsimile":218,"letterHeights":219,"publications":223,"zotero":227,"keywords":231},"Fragment of a monumental Greek inscription",{"_":5},"edited",[7,10,12,14,16],{"_":8,"type":9},"644948","TM",{"type":11},"EDR",{"type":13},"EDH",{"type":15},"EDCS",{"_":17,"type":18},"140309","PHI",null,{"_":21,"ana":22,"ref":23,"cert":24},"building","#function.building","https://ontology.inscriptiones.org/type_of_inscription/Building_inscription","low","A large block of compact limestone (described by Orsi as 'calcare di Canicattini'), rectangular, chiselled roughly flat on each side. Note that Orsi's measurements in the Taccuini report a depth of 90 cm, but he also states that when it was removed from its location in the Ortygia fortifications it was 'segata' prior to transportation to the museum; so the inference must be that the rear two-thirds of the block were cut away prior to transportation.",{"_":27,"ana":28,"ref":29},"block","#object.block","http://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/objtyp/lod/189.html",{"_":31,"type":32,"subtype":33,"ref":35},"limestone","inorganic.stone",[34],"unverified","http://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/material/lod/66.html",{"ana":37},"#condition.fragment",[39,43,46],{"_":40,"unit":41,"dimension":42},"37","cm","height",{"_":44,"unit":41,"dimension":45},"71","width",{"_":47,"unit":41,"dimension":48},"30.5-31.5","depth",{"layout":50},{"p":51,"rs":52,"damage":60},"A single line of monumental letters across the broad face of the block, with more space above (11.5cm) than below. Traces of red paint on a white plaster ground visible in the kappa.",[53,57],{"_":54,"ana":55,"ref":56},"chiselled","#execution.chiselled","http://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/writing/lod/1",{"_":58,"ana":59},"Rubrication, red","#execution.rubrication.red",{"ana":61},"#text_condition.incomplete",{"lettering":63,"dimensions":64},"Elegant deep (14mm), v-cut letters of regular form. Kappa with short equal arms; sigma deep with slightly outward curving top and bottom strokes; alpha wide with straight bar.",[65,73],{"type":66,"l":67,"from":68,"to":68,"h":69,"unit":70,"atLeast":71,"atMost":72},"letterHeight","Line 1","line1","185-205","mm","185","205",{"type":74,"l":75,"from":68,"to":76,"h":77,"unit":70},"interlinear","Interlineation line 1 to 2","line2","NA",{"_":79,"notBefore":80,"notAfter":81,"evidence":82},"3rd century BCE",-300,-201,"lettering",[84,89],{"_":85,"type":86,"ref":87,"region":88},"Syracusae","ancient","http://pleiades.stoa.org/places/462503","Sicilia",{"_":90,"type":91,"ref":92,"region":88},"Siracusa","modern","http://sws.geonames.org/2523083",[94],[95,96],37.08415,15.27628,{"_":98,"type":99,"subtype":100,"when":101,"geo":102},"Ortygia, extracted from the wall bordering the last canal/ditch linking the great and small harbours, on the corner looking towards the great harbour, in late 1888, at which point noted and recorded by Orsi, and transfered to the museum 4 December 1888; recently relocated in store in the archaeological park of Neapolis.","found","discovered","1888",[103,104],37.0626632,15.288339,[103,104],{"_":107,"type":108,"subtype":109,"xml:id":110,"geo":19},"Prag 2026-09-17, in storage in the Neapolis archaeological park.","observed","autopsied","autopsy",[112,119,124,127,130],{"n":113,"url":114,"height":115,"width":116,"desc":117,"surfaceType":118},"screen","ISic003403_tiled.tif","3680px","5520px","I.Sicily with the permission of the Assessorato Regionale dei Beni Culturali e dell’Identità Siciliana - Dipartimento dei Beni Culturali e dell’Identità Siciliana; photo J. Prag 2026-09-17","front",{"n":113,"url":120,"height":121,"width":122,"desc":117,"surfaceType":123},"ISic003403_top_tiled.tif","2268px","4032px","top",{"n":113,"url":125,"height":121,"width":122,"desc":117,"surfaceType":126},"ISic003403_left_tiled.tif","left",{"n":113,"url":128,"height":121,"width":122,"desc":117,"surfaceType":129},"ISic003403_right_tiled.tif","right",{"n":113,"url":131,"height":121,"width":122,"desc":117,"surfaceType":132},"ISic003403_rear_tiled.tif","rear","Sicily",{"_":135,"role":136,"ref":137,"museum":138},"Museo Archeologico Regionale Paolo Orsi","museum","http://sicily.classics.ox.ac.uk/museum/097",{"slug":139,"type":136,"name":135,"uri":137,"description":140,"location":141},"097","An outstanding collection of archaeological material. The collection ranges from Siracusa and the surrounding territory (Megara Hyblaia, Akrai, Kasmenai etc) to encompass all of eastern Sicily, reaching as far as Gela and Agrigento. The ground floor covers prehistory through to the end of the Classical period. Upstairs includes Hellenistic and Roman Syracuse and a display of material from the catacombs. A gallery displaying material from Hellenistic eastern Sicily is in preparation.",{"settlement":90,"region":90,"country":142,"address":143,"geo":144},"Italy","Viale Teocrito 66, 96100 - Siracusa",{"lat":145,"lon":146},37.07636989,15.2866213,{"_":148,"type":149},"12254","inventory",{"_":151,"mainLang":152,"languages":153},"Ancient Greek","grc",[151],{"type":155,"bibl":156},"edition",[157,171,184],{"type":158,"n":159,"author":160,"date":161,"citedRange":162,"ptr":166,"ref":167,"inscriptionDate":161,"title":168,"citation":169,"uri":170,"year":161},"corpus","IG","Kaibel","1890",{"ref":163},{"_":164,"target":165},"15b","https://clio.columbia.edu/catalog/6873760",{"target":167},"htt